Modification: scripts/fetch.mjs adds patches/shadow_observe.rs as a new
Windows module. This extends the real WindowsAdapter with restricted,
password-first observation and root identity APIs. It does not replace or
silently claim the safety of the unmodified get_tree implementation.

Retain upstream LICENSE and any upstream notices in binary distributions.
Audit and include third-party dependency licenses with each actual release;
this source milestone has not generated a complete dependency license bundle.

The restricted module now also contains the exact single-pattern UIA action and
foreground target/focus/ancestry verification APIs. The native bridge uses an
independent shadow-input-guard.exe artifact for approved physical input, not
upstream's keyboard_send/mouse_send paths.

shadow-input-guard.exe is AOT-compiled from the existing Shadow source
src/execution/computer/windows-input.cs by scripts/agent-desktop-input-guard.ts,
with the old runtime PowerShell launcher removed and named-event cancellation
added. That existing Shadow C# source is distinct from agent-desktop upstream;
the upstream Apache-2.0 notice does not automatically relicense that source or
the guard binary under Apache-2.0. Distribution must retain applicable Shadow
repository/source licensing and notices in addition to upstream/dependency ones.
The guard also requires the Windows .NET Framework runtime/system assemblies;
these are system prerequisites, not bundled upstream Apache-licensed code.
